# G9 (graphics): the file dialog's Open. Folders, files, sizes and dates of a disk, the places, the type drop-down, the sort arrow,
# type-ahead, a folder entered and left, Look in and a file taken by its name. No frame lists the drive's root, where DOS keeps
# the DPMI swap file with the real date. Every frame's CRC-32 must equal the host's in both
# graphics modes (the keys are played from a file: the dialog needs Alt chords, which AUTOTYPE cannot hold).
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\DOCS
@dir DOCS\LETTERS\OLD
@dir DOCS\2025
@dir QUILL\SAMPLES
@copy letter.qld DOCS\
@copy letter.rtf DOCS\
@copy plain.qld DOCS\
@copy pic.bmp DOCS\
@copy wide.rtf DOCS\
@copy lists.rtf DOCS\LETTERS\
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.QLD 2026-11-24 18:45
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.RTF 2026-11-02 09:05
@stamp DOCS\PLAIN.QLD 2026-03-14 12:00
@stamp DOCS\PIC.BMP 2025-10-01 08:30
@stamp DOCS\WIDE.RTF 2026-05-02 14:30
@place Samples C:\QUILL\SAMPLES
f10 down enter                # File > Open...
altt f4                       # Files of type: the drop-down
end enter                     # All Files
altl down down down           # the list: 2025, LETTERS, then the first file; its name goes in the field
alt2 alt2                     # sort by size, then largest first
alt3                          # by date
alt1                          # by name again
l                             # type-ahead: LETTERS ...
l                             # ... and the next entry that starts with L
@wait 10
p                             # a new prefix after ten ticks: PIC.BMP
altn l e t t e r              # a name typed in the field
altl home down down enter     # the list: into LETTERS
bspace                        # back up to DOCS
alti f4                       # Look in: the drop-down
down esc                      # closed again
altp end enter                # the Samples place: C:\QUILL\SAMPLES
altp home enter               # the C: place: its own folder, C:\DOCS
altn end bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace   # the typed name emptied
p l a i n period q l d enter  # opens DOCS\PLAIN.QLD by its name
